ia and going to the restroom without caregiver supervision. This was corrected during the inspection when the children returned to the cafeteria and the caregivers were notified that children need to be supervised when they leave the cafeteria.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026513482","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §744.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1391177-i20240418-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-744-1309-d","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1391177-i20240418","date":"2024-04-18","original_code":"744.1309(d)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-05-24","finding":"Documented Annual Training-Required Topics in Health and Safety: Out of two staff files reviewed, one did not have training in communicable diseases, emergency preparedness, preventing food allergy reactions, understanding building and physical premises safety, and handling hazardous materials.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026312804","violation_type_title":"Documented Annual Training-Required Topics in Health and Safety (26 TAC §744.1309(d))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1391177-i20240418-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-744-901","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1391177-i20240418","date":"2024-04-18","original_code":"744.901","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-05-24","finding":"Required Personnel Records: Out of the two staff files reviewed, one did not have proof of education on file and one did not have statements that she had received copies of the operational and personnel policies.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026272528","violation_type_title":"Required Personnel Records (26 TAC §744.901)","topic_label":"Sup